{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774749,"nonce":"xKdQwYyA+9Xe4A/wd4UCCUyDp88=","title":"The keyed directory Cache: warm-only, explicit, never evidence (dbe05e5)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #103 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/dbe05e5-keyed-cache` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-08-26T07:30:13Z · Merged: 2026-08-26T12:44:58Z\n\nThe keyed directory Cache (git-bug `dbe05e5`, ADR-0065 s1) — **warm-only by owner decision**, with the evidence bar for ever going durable written into the ADR note. **911/911 green.** Full chain: design → skeptical audit (2 BLOCKS caught) → independent judge (overruled one of my calls — integrity failures 422, never drop-and-warn) → build → review (all five amendments verified in the diff).\n\n**What it is:** `cache: { dirs: [node_modules], key: [package-lock.json] }` on a step. Restore at start, save at end, keyed by the lockfile's blob hash — computed by the control plane from tree entries alone (no content reads). Explicit, per-project, never shared mutable, never evidence: **a miss is slower, never wrong** — pinned by an e2e that wipes warm and asserts identical output identity.\n\n**The security posture (this is a cross-run content-injection surface, and was reviewed as one):**\n- Restore rides the token's existing exact-roots claim — zero new auth surface; the pod never queries by key.\n- The mapping's trust root is closed: `post_drain` 422s the whole drain if a reported cache root isn't in the fence's **own** write ledger (judge's ruling: integrity is never best-effort; a tripped check is compromise or a serious bug, both fail loudly).\n- **PR-context runs (fork or same-repo) cannot write cache entries**; they read freely. Push rights already imply pipeline-edit rights, so branch-push writes add no capability.\n- Validation rejects `.`/`.git*`/overlapping dirs/outputs∩cache overlap; the fetcher restores only into a dir absent-or-empty after source materialize — **source wins**, always.\n\n**Honesty:** cache hits assume `replicaCount=1` — at N\u003e1 the effective hit rate is ~`(1/N)^files` (no cold copy; blob GETs scatter independently). Follow-up ticketed as `12e2f6b` (affinity-routed restores vs durable copies, priced with that arithmetic). This feature also makes `cba7165` (the warm space bound) strictly more urgent.\n\nSave/restore/upsert are best-effort in every arm except the integrity check; cache subtrees never consume pack rows (pack-absence test). Migration 0049. `DrainRecord` evolves additively. Review nits, non-blocking: a stale \"display/audit only\" comment on origin stamping (it now gates cache writes), and `cache.dirs` is uncapped (same shape as `outputs:`).\n\nCloses `dbe05e5` on merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}